{{Unobtainable}}
'''Redhead Yuki Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that could be obtained when beating any stage in [[Shoumetsu Toshi Collaboration Event#The Lost World|The Lost World]] during the [[Shoumetsu Toshi Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 6.1 Update|Version 6.1]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]] gains the ability to perform [[Surge Attack]]s.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 340
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Redhead Yuki Cat
|name2 = Redhead Lovely Yuki Cat
|name3 = Redhead Muscled Yuki Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Redhead Lovely Yuki Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Redhead Muscled Yuki Cat''' when obtained from [[Redhead Yuki Cat Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
This unit is a low-quality [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] ripoff. In comparison to Neo Psychocat, her advantages are higher movement speed, slightly faster attack rate, 10 frames less recharge time and being able to freeze instead of slow. That's it. Psychocat's more-than-doubled HP and significantly higher proc rate make Redhead Yuki completely outclassed against Aliens, and she is even less useful than Psychocat as a generalist. Not to mention, Corrupted Psychocat eliminates both the speed and attack rate advantages, and these are both Rare Units so she doesn't have any usage within restrictions that Psychocat doesn't. Overall, she should only really be used if you don't yet have Psychocat and are struggling in [[Into the Future]].

==='''True Form'''===
Surge Attacks can increase Yuki Cat's uptime and freeze enemies in the backlines, in addition offering a pseudo-Area Attack at times, but it is inconsistent, especially due to still relying on her middling proc rate and being remarkably fragile.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & User Rank Dump}}

